r  series creator as a showrunner whatever  you want to call him this question first  the episode opens with a glimpse of some  enormous piece of machinery and there  seems to be a big answer  hidden in there is this mystery  something we can expect to be solved  this season SML answers and this is I'm  reading this directly from the article  white roses motivation has always been  shrouded in a lot of mystery for those  last two seasons even though I didn't  want to answer exactly what it was I  wanted to at least show the thing and I  wanted to drill down on her obsession to  control her reality visa vie this  technology she's producing that  parallels any real-life billionaire in  our world who's obsessed with technology  and makes these lofty claims whether  it's anti-aging or singularity or AI or  space we kind of wanted to model white  roses Ark on that level  what if someone with extreme wealth and  resources had this goal of being able to  control their own reality and they  really wanted to execute that through  technology that's as much as we want to  reveal right now the audience we're  going to give out more details later it  was important to set that up this season  because I think we've been teasing it  long enough we thought it was important  to at least show the thing even if  you're not exactly clear on what you're  seeing the interviewer then followed up  was a time travel question he said just  as a general question totally  disconnected from mr. robot do you think  season 3 of a television show is too  late to introduce the concept of time  travel  Sam SML answered and he was laughing he  says the problem with time travel I've  always said in the writers room that  whenever you introduce time travel it's  game over then all the rules go out the  window throwing out time travel in the  middle of a series run is a little late  now this isn't an actual flat-out denial  but I think it is a denial just the same  and I mentioned in my episode one recap  and review that I just never have seen  it going that way I followed most of the  theories on reddit and other places and  I've read them all there like I said  there's plenty of compelling ones I just  haven't adopted any of them as what I  think the show is going to do I could be  wrong but I  don't think so and I think this actually  backs that up I do think what he said  about White Rose is a lot more  interesting and I think it's a lot more  relevant to what's going on  in our lifetime wealth redistribution  going up to the top is something that's  been going on pretty consistently for  the past 40 years of course there's been  other periods in our history where  there's been that same kind of massive  wealth at the top but I mean there's  just a lot of billionaires out there now  and there's some of them are a little  bit wacky I'm not going to talk about  anybody in particular but when you get  into billions of dollars and tens of  billions of dollars you know that is an  amazing amount of resources and  whiterose is a pretty interesting  character because we know that there is  a real command of Technology there so I  really like this little nugget that he  threw out I think it's interesting I  would love to hear your theories about  what you think White Rose is up to I  think it does actually tie into that  thing being underneath the ground in New  Jersey as well I think that is the  Washington Township plant and that is  why White Rose is so obsessed with that  area but time will tell we don't know  for sure yet and that's about it for  this video thanks for watching please  like the video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already  my next mr. robot video is going to be  Easter egg related it's gonna be a  collection of all the little things you  might have missed in the episode there  were quite a few prominent things that  stood out to me on first watch that I  didn't mention in my recap there is a  real noticeable QR co